  <h1>Gaurav Srivastava</h1>
  <p class="lead">An independent thinker and writer on how to live and lead well in demanding times. He moves easily from the inner life to hard practical choices.</p>
  <p>He spent two decades in the technology industry and built his own consulting company before selling it to a larger firm. He is a restless learner with a devotional streak who would rather be useful than clever.</p>
  <p>His books tend to begin the same way: he sets out to understand a subject that has caught him, spends months on the research, and lets his own experience shape what it becomes. Each book is the one he wishes he had found sooner.</p>
